SWEET AMP TONE (patch 0172, plan A10), on top of 0171 (boot-arg sweetaoc=7 + sweetamp=1). USER DECISION 2026-11-18 ("Change that rule and ignore
safety checks for now"): the rule "PLL locked + reviewed calibration before GLOBAL_EN" and the tone bounds are lifted for this level only. As
sweetaoc=6 (HALO fw load + start, AOC stream), then, while both cores run and the stream runs: the stock CS35L41 power-up in DAPM order (PCM
Source DSP, boost enable, ASPRX1/2 + unmute, VMON/IMON/VPMON/VBSTMON/TEMPMON ADCs, DSP1 RESUME mailbox, AMP_EN, pup patch, MBOX_8 := 0,
GLOBAL_EN, 1 ms, PUP_DONE <= 100 ms, PLL_LOCK <= 100 ms, IRQ1_STATUS1 error bits), a 5.4 s tone window (the glue feeds three 1 s beeps of a 1 kHz
sine, 1 s apart, -30.0 dBFS, into audio_playback0; IRQ1_STATUS1 of both amps every 50 ms, an error bit ends it), then the stock power-down
(mute, ADCs off, AMP_EN off, PAUSE, MBOX_8 := 0, GLOBAL_EN := 0 + PDN_DONE <= 100 ms, pdn patch, ASPRX off, mixer words back, read back) on
every path after the first write; then the 0169 window 2, DSP stop, SOURCE off, BIND2 off, amp reset (restore). Sources cited in
bsd/dev/sweet_amp_pwr.h (AMP cs35l41.c / cs35l41.h / tables, Linux v6.18 cs35l41-lib.c, DAPM soc-dapm.c ordering). PWR_CTRL1 and the power
words pass amp_write_ok only while armed by amp_pwr_w for exactly that (register, value); levels <= 6 never arm it. The tone starts 75 s after
"AOC online" (SWAU_TONE_DELAY_S). Lines: "SWEET AUDIO: amp on l,r pll ...", "SWEET AUDIO: tone played N bytes ..., amp off l,r, errors none",
"SWEET AMP: L|R pwr ..." (IRQ1_STATUS1 pre/up/tone/end, IRQ1_STATUS3, mailbox status, PUP/PLL/PDN, end PWR_CTRL1/2, SP_ENABLES, volume words).
Host tests: aoc_audio_host_test (tone pattern), amp_xnu_host_test (PWR_CTRL1 armed-only). No Linux code copied.

